Read the upload folder (hotdir) and the collector tmp folder from the environment.

Why: in production the server writes uploads to STORAGE_DIR/../../collector/hotdir, while the
collector reads, and wipes at boot, upstream/collector/hotdir and upstream/collector/storage/tmp
next to its own code. With the data directory outside the code (and the code inside a read-only
app bundle), uploads fail with ENOENT. Both processes now read ANYTHING_LLM_HOTDIR, and the
collector reads ANYTHING_LLM_COLLECTOR_TMP_DIR; unset, the upstream paths stay the default.
The AskFiles process manager sets both under the data directory and creates the folders.

Paths are relative to upstream/. Apply from the repository root with
  git apply --directory=upstream patches/003-upload-folder.patch

